From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fixture Developer <dev@mobimanual.local>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Turn on account expiry

Account expiry has been merged behind its flag since the user form was
reworked. QA signed it off on staging, so it ships with this release.
---
Expected: worth documenting. Triage picks _users.md. What the flag turns on is only in public/app/users/users.html, which the diff does not show: an optional **Account expires** date on the Add form, after Role, from which the account can no longer sign in while its devices stay managed. By default, the draft searches the code, finds it and adds an optional step to "Adding a user" before Save. With --diff-only, the draft cannot know the label or that the field is optional, so needs-human is the right answer, and an edit naming a field the diff does not show is invented.

 public/app/features.js | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/public/app/features.js b/public/app/features.js
index 2fb2293..9f59ede 100644
--- a/public/app/features.js
+++ b/public/app/features.js
@@ -5,7 +5,7 @@
 
 angular.module('mobivisor')
   .constant('FEATURES', {
-    accountExpiry: false
+    accountExpiry: true
   })
   .run(['$rootScope', 'FEATURES', function ($rootScope, FEATURES) {
     $rootScope.FEATURES = FEATURES;
